    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0676" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2289: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schuyler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-31T17:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 2—10:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. In reply to your telegram January 30, 6 p.m., the President states that he has
                    been and is taking every possible precaution and telegraphing orders to
                    departmental commanders to arrest any persons attempting revolutionary
                    activities against Honduras. It seems a band of 40 men armed with machetes has
                    been observed on the <pb facs="0677" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/> frontier of Gotera
                    and orders have now been given to capture them. The only Honduran leader of
                    importance now in this city will be arrested this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Flores is personal representative of Orellana<anchor n="6" xml:id="d484-f1"/> not
                    of the President of Salvador and is now in this city (see my confidential
                    despatch 103, January 6th, page 3,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d484-f2"/> and my
                    telegram January 11, 9 p.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d484-f3"/>).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
